Scope and decisions:
Create a bounded isolated coding-environment spike using a real repository, actual commands and actual durable storage, separate from publisher/checker environments. Cloudflare provider documentation describes ephemeral disk and snapshots that exclude processes; a stable sandbox ID or periodic checkpoint is insufficient evidence of Artroom durability. Use an authoritative quiesced project backup in owned R2, containing working tree, index, refs, Git object bytes, modes, symlinks, tracked deletions and untracked files. Commit its immutable manifest before acknowledging an edit or completed mutating command. Serialize mutations and stop or fence background writers at a checkpoint. Verify restore into ordinary filesystem storage; do not assume an R2 mount has POSIX Git semantics.
Persist edit intent/content/base/result hashes before apply; persist command intent before dispatch, sequenced redacted outputs and terminal exit/checkpoint receipts. Persist prepared commit bytes and exact OID before acknowledgement; persist fork-push destination, expected old OID, prepared OID and workspace epoch before dispatch. Reattach running commands only by matching execution-instance and job ID. Execution-host loss ends processes; it does not authorize replay of arbitrary shell, install scripts or external writes. A declared safe read-only check can run as a new attempt. Reconcile unknown command/push results through observation and durable attention. Missing/corrupt checkpoints must fail recovery visibly.
Record provider/SDK version, bounded resource/spend limits, commands, wall time and actual cost. Demonstrate credential/network separation and lease/epoch write fencing. Seven-day owned backup retention is a configurable default; provider snapshots without explicit delete remain optional warm cache with their own visible retention. Deliver findings and executable probe, not a production runtime or a new whole-repository suite.
Apply the reconciled design decisions, not Draft1 wording: existing sessions are read-only; controls use signed resource/action-bound current owner/admin requests. Initially one new agent member and one DO/conversation/lane per task; no in-place owner reassignment. Last-active-owner-key revocation or owner removal stops new tools/broker writes/renewals; another active owner device keeps independent-agent work alive. Admins retain private export/settlement, and lost-key recovery restores only an active member, never a removed handle. Optional delegated agent mode is not required in initial runtime delivery; its key-bound grantor rules and conditional acceptance remain specified. Render repository/command output inert in the key-owning origin and expose only minimal activity to other Room readers.
Saved root includes ignored/generated/dependency project files and self-contained Git storage; external Git alternates/directories are dissociated into owned storage or refused, symlinks are not followed outside, special files fail saves explicitly, and out-of-root persistent work is unsupported initially. Quiesce detached child writers. Persist/verify all payload and object closure before manifest; atomically commit receipt/current checkpoint under current epoch/instance/base, then ack. Preserve the last good checkpoint on limits/save failure, separating observed exit from durable result. Old callbacks cannot replace a new current receipt/pointer/commit. A new command attempt has a distinct linked ID and never closes the old unknown duty. Pin bytes/objects needed by outstanding effects; legally expire checkpoint/export roots in a durable purge transaction and return explicit expired/unknown on old-ID retries after permitted deletion.

