Acceptance outcome:
Edit tracked and untracked files, delete a tracked path, complete one mutating command and prepare an unpushed commit. Abruptly kill the execution host and restart its controller; restore all acknowledged files, command receipt and exact Git OID. Interrupt one non-replayable side effect after dispatch; show unknown/reconciliation without duplicating it. Lose a fork-push reply and recover one expected remote head by readback/CAS. Fence a stale epoch after takeover and keep the former holder's private checkpoint separate. Verify one owned payload deletion and durable retry of a failed deletion. Report any inability to meet these invariants without weakening the user story. Include one detached writer, stale save callback and failed save retaining the prior good checkpoint. A second authorized command attempt leaves the first unknown duty open; purge preserves required pins and a legally deleted result returns expired rather than dispatching anew.

